## Introduction
When people talk about trash pollution, the conversation usually stays abstract—“plastic in the ocean,” “litter on the beach,” “microplastics everywhere.” This dataset makes the problem feel concrete. It records individual dumpster “collections” of trash over time (2014–2023), measuring not just total weight (tons) and volume (cubic yards), but also specific item counts like plastic bottles, cigarette butts, wrappers, and plastic bags.
